+# Threshold Feature - Implementation Summary
+
+## What Was Implemented
+
+Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option to `frai eval` command that gates evaluation on metric scores, allowing CI pipelines to fail when quality thresholds aren't met.
+
+## Files Modified
+
+### frai-core (SDK library)
+
+**`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`**
+- Added `validateThresholds(thresholds, validMetricIds)` function
+  - Validates metric IDs exist in the evaluation results
+  - Validates threshold values are numbers between 0 and 1
+  - Returns `{valid: boolean, errors?: string[]}`
+  
+- Updated `generateReport(config)` signature
+  - Now accepts optional `thresholds` parameter
+  - Builds array of threshold results: `{metric, min, score, passed}`
+  - Adds `passed` boolean (true if all thresholds met or null score) to report
+  - Throws `THRESHOLD_VALIDATION_ERROR` with details and validMetricIds on validation failure
+  - Maintains backward compatibility (no new fields when thresholds not provided)
+
+**`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`**
+- Updated `toMarkdown(report)` function
+  - Adds "## Thresholds" section before metrics (when thresholds present)
+  - Shows format: `- **metric_id:** PASS/FAIL (score: X, min: Y)`
+  - JSON reporter unchanged (serializes new fields automatically)
+
+**`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`**
+- Added 8 comprehensive tests:
+  - ✓ Thresholds pass when scores meet minimum
+  - ✓ Thresholds fail when scores below minimum
+  - ✓ Null scores always fail thresholds
+  - ✓ Unknown metric IDs rejected with validation error
+  - ✓ Invalid threshold values (outside 0-1) rejected
+  - ✓ Markdown report includes threshold section
+  - ✓ Backward compatibility (no thresholds = no new fields)
+  - (Existing tests still pass)
+
+### frai-cli (Command-line interface)
+
+**`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`**
+
+- Updated `EvalOptions` interface
+  - Added `threshold?: string[]` field
+
+- Added `parseThresholds(thresholdStrs?: string[])` function
+  - Parses CLI args like `exact_match=0.9` into object
+  - Uses regex `/^([a-z_]+)=([0-9]*\.?[0-9]+)$/` (strict number format)
+  - Rejects malformed inputs (missing value, wrong format)
+  - Validates range is 0-1 after parsing
+  - Returns `Record<string, number>` or null
+  - Throws error with user-friendly message on validation failure
+
+- Updated `runEvalCommand(options)` function
+  - Parse thresholds before other processing (fail fast)
+  - Exit code 2 if threshold parsing fails
+  - Call `generateReport()` with parsed thresholds
+  - Catch `THRESHOLD_VALIDATION_ERROR` specifically
+    - Print error + list of valid metric IDs
+    - Exit code 2
+  - Always write report before evaluating pass/fail
+  - Exit code 1 if thresholds provided and not passed
+  - Exit code 0 if all thresholds pass (or no thresholds)
+
+- Updated `eval` command definition
+  - Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option
+  - Implemented accumulator function for multiple values
+  - Each `--threshold` adds to array
+
+## Behavior
+
+### Command Usage
+
+```bash
+# Single threshold
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+
+# Multiple thresholds
+frai eval \
+  --outputs outputs.json \
+  --references refs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \
+  --threshold toxicity=0.95 \
+  --format markdown
+
+# In CI
+if frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold exact_match=0.8; then
+  echo "Passed"
+else
+  echo "Failed with code $?"
+fi
+```
+
+### Exit Codes
+
+- **0**: All thresholds pass, or no thresholds specified
+- **1**: One or more thresholds failed (report written)
+- **2**: Validation error (invalid format, invalid value, unknown metric; no report written)
+
+### Threshold Validation
+
+- Format: `<metric_id>=<number>`
+- Valid metrics: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`, plus custom metrics
+- Valid values: Any number from 0 to 1 (e.g., `0`, `0.5`, `.5`, `1`)
+- Invalid: `0.9.5` (multiple dots), `1.5` (out of range), `foo=bar` (not a number)
+
+### Report Output
+
+**JSON** (when thresholds provided):
+```json
+{
+  "passed": false,
+  "thresholds": [
+    {"metric": "exact_match", "min": 0.9, "score": 0.66, "passed": false},
+    {"metric": "toxicity", "min": 0.95, "score": 1.0, "passed": true}
+  ],
+  "metadata": {...},
+  "metrics": [...]
+}
+```
+
+**Markdown** (when thresholds provided):
+```
+# FRAI Evaluation Report
+
+...
+
+## Thresholds
+
+- **exact_match:** FAIL (score: 0.66, min: 0.9)
+- **toxicity:** PASS (score: 1.0, min: 0.95)
+
+## Metrics
+
+### Exact Match
+...
+```
+
+## Error Handling Examples
+
+```bash
+# Error: malformed format
+$ frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold "exact_match 0.9"
+[...] ERROR Malformed threshold: exact_match 0.9. Expected format: <metric>=<number>
+# Exits with code 2
+
+# Error: value out of range
+$ frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold exact_match=1.5
+[...] ERROR Invalid threshold value for exact_match: 1.5. Minimum must be a number between 0 and 1.
+# Exits with code 2
+
+# Error: unknown metric
+$ frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold unknown_metric=0.5
+[...] ERROR Invalid threshold metric. Valid metrics are:
+  - exact_match
+  - toxicity
+  - length_variance
+  Error: Unknown metric id: unknown_metric
+# Exits with code 2
+
+# Error: threshold not met
+$ frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold exact_match=0.95
+[...] SUCCESS Evaluation report generated. { path: '/path/to/frai-eval-report.json' }
+# Exits with code 1 (report was written)
+```
+
+## SDK Usage
+
+```javascript
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({
+  outputs: ['hello', 'world'],
+  references: ['hello', 'world']
+});
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: 'outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: 'refs.json',
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.95
+  }
+});
+
+if (report.passed === false) {
+  console.error('Some thresholds failed:');
+  report.thresholds.forEach(t => {
+    console.error(`  ${t.metric}: ${t.passed ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'} (${t.score}/${t.min})`);
+  });
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+- Without `--threshold` flags, CLI behavior is identical to previous version
+- SDK users not using the `thresholds` parameter are unaffected
+- Reports without thresholds don't include `passed` or `thresholds` fields
+- Existing workflows continue unchanged
+
+## Documentation Updates
+
+- **README.md**: Added `--threshold` option to `frai eval` section with exit code details
+- **docs/eval_harness_design.md**: Added threshold support to MVP Scope
+- **THRESHOLD_FEATURE.md**: Detailed feature documentation (this directory)
+
+## Testing
+
+Tests verify:
+- ✓ Threshold passing logic
+- ✓ Threshold failing logic
+- ✓ Null score handling
+- ✓ Unknown metric rejection
+- ✓ Invalid value rejection
+- ✓ Markdown formatting
+- ✓ Backward compatibility
+- ✓ Error codes and messages (CLI)
+- ✓ Report writing (always happens before exit)
+
+Run with: `npm test` or `pnpm test`
+
+## Notes
+
+- Multiple thresholds for the same metric: last one wins (dict key overwrite)
+- Metrics with no score always fail thresholds (expected behavior per spec)
+- Custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations` are automatically supported for thresholds
+- Report is written before evaluating pass/fail (ensures evidence is saved)
