+# Threshold Feature Implementation
+
+## Overview
+Added threshold support to `frai eval` that allows CI pipelines to fail/pass based on metric scores.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. Core Library (frai-core)
+
+#### `/packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`
+- Added `validateThresholds()` helper to validate threshold configurations
+- Modified `generateReport()` to:
+  - Accept optional `thresholds` parameter: `{ metric_id: min_score, ... }`
+  - Validate thresholds against available metrics and value ranges (0-1)
+  - Return `passed` field (boolean) when thresholds are provided
+  - Return `thresholds` array with `{metric, min, score, passed}` entries
+  - Throw `THRESHOLD_VALIDATION_ERROR` on invalid thresholds with details
+- Report structure unchanged when no thresholds provided (backward compatible)
+
+#### `/packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`
+- Updated `toMarkdown()` to include "## Thresholds" section when thresholds are present
+- Shows `PASS` or `FAIL` status for each threshold with score and min values
+- Format: `- **metric_id:** PASS (score: 0.95, min: 0.9)`
+
+#### `/packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`
+- Added 8 new tests covering:
+  - Passing thresholds
+  - Failing thresholds
+  - Null scores causing threshold failures
+  - Unknown metric rejection
+  - Invalid threshold values rejection
+  - Markdown formatting
+  - Backward compatibility (no thresholds = no new fields)
+
+### 2. CLI (frai-cli)
+
+#### `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`
+- Updated `EvalOptions` interface to accept `threshold?: string[]`
+- Added `parseThresholds()` function to parse CLI args like `exact_match=0.9`
+  - Validates format: `<metric_id>=<number>`
+  - Validates range: 0 to 1 inclusive
+  - Returns `Record<string, number>` or null
+- Modified `runEvalCommand()` to:
+  - Parse and validate CLI thresholds before report generation
+  - Exit 2 if threshold parsing fails (invalid format or value)
+  - Exit 2 if threshold validation fails with list of valid metric IDs
+  - Exit 1 if evaluation thresholds are not met
+  - Exit 0 if all thresholds pass (or no thresholds specified)
+  - Always write report regardless of outcome
+- Updated `eval` command definition to include `--threshold` option
+  - Can be used multiple times: `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`
+
+### 3. Documentation
+
+#### `/README.md`
+- Updated `frai eval` section with `--threshold` option documentation
+- Explains exit codes: 0 (pass/no thresholds), 1 (fail), 2 (validation error)
+- Notes that reports include threshold results
+
+#### `/docs/eval_harness_design.md`
+- Added thresholds to MVP Scope
+- Mentions gating capability and exit codes
+
+## Behavior
+
+### Threshold Validation
+- Format: `<metric_id>=<number>` (e.g., `exact_match=0.9`)
+- Valid metrics: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`, plus any custom metrics
+- Valid range: 0 to 1 inclusive
+- Multiple thresholds can be specified: `--threshold m1=0.8 --threshold m2=0.7`
+
+### Exit Codes
+- **0**: Success (all thresholds pass, or no thresholds specified)
+- **1**: Failure (one or more thresholds not met; report still written)
+- **2**: Validation error (malformed threshold, invalid value, unknown metric; no report written)
+
+### Null Scores
+- If a metric has no score (e.g., exact_match without references), threshold always fails
+- Reported as `{metric, min, score: null, passed: false}`
+
+### Report Output
+When thresholds are provided:
+- **JSON**: Top-level `passed` boolean + `thresholds` array
+- **Markdown**: New "## Thresholds" section before metrics
+
+Example JSON:
+```json
+{
+  "passed": false,
+  "thresholds": [
+    {"metric": "exact_match", "min": 0.9, "score": 0.66, "passed": false},
+    {"metric": "toxicity", "min": 0.95, "score": 1.0, "passed": true}
+  ],
+  "metadata": {...},
+  "metrics": [...]
+}
+```
+
+Example Markdown:
+```
+## Thresholds
+
+- **exact_match:** FAIL (score: 0.66, min: 0.9)
+- **toxicity:** PASS (score: 1.0, min: 0.95)
+
+## Metrics
+...
+```
+
+## CLI Examples
+
+```bash
+# Single threshold
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+
+# Multiple thresholds
+frai eval \
+  --outputs outputs.json \
+  --references refs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \
+  --threshold toxicity=0.95 \
+  --format markdown
+
+# With custom report path
+frai eval \
+  --outputs outputs.json \
+  --references refs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.8 \
+  --report evaluation
+
+# In CI pipeline
+if frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9; then
+  echo "Evaluation passed"
+else
+  echo "Evaluation failed"
+fi
+```
+
+## SDK Usage
+
+```typescript
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({
+  outputs: [...],
+  references: [...]
+});
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: 'outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: 'refs.json',
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.95
+  }
+});
+
+console.log(report.passed); // false if any threshold fails
+console.log(report.thresholds); // Array of {metric, min, score, passed}
+
+if (report.passed === false) {
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
+## Testing
+
+Run tests with:
+```bash
+npm test  # or pnpm test
+```
+
+Tests verify:
+- Threshold parsing and validation
+- Report generation with thresholds
+- Exit codes in CLI
+- Markdown and JSON formatting
+- Null score handling
+- Error messages for invalid inputs
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+- Without `--threshold` flags, behavior is identical to before
+- Reports without thresholds don't include `passed` or `thresholds` fields
+- SDK users without the `thresholds` parameter are unaffected
+- Existing evaluation workflows continue to work unchanged
